    "finding": "The published inputs.census.git_blob_sha1 value 9c251da3138c5cb0516e097be5e5d35ab4f26a5d is not the git blob SHA-1 of any file in this repository. It is a splice of the first 29 hex characters of the census file's git blob SHA-1 with the last 11 hex characters of the K0863 knowledge item's git blob SHA-1 (c2ae353cab4a7dbcd28ec53b0f57d35ab4f26a5d). The correct git blob SHA-1 of research/experiments/n11-head1410-receipt-unclosability-census-20261116/output/n11-head1410-receipt-unclosability-census-20261116.json is 9c251da3138c5cb0516e097be5e5d0427dfaf5f0 (single-commit file history on main; the same correct pin is used by all earlier publications of this experiment). The published verifier crosscheck_cost16_parent_shared_memo_20261118.py carried the same spliced pin and would abort at the census pin check on a repo checkout; the script pin was corrected in place in the same commit as this amendment. The A16/B16/total values in this record are unaffected by the pin defect: they agree with the checkpoint computation and the pinned phase-A output, and are re-verified by an independent implementation in the companion experiment of the same commit.",
